{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"8881a0cf9522c615","type":"group","x":-180,"y":-480,"width":2320,"height":1495,"label":"Untitled group"},
		{"id":"title","type":"text","text":"# DigiDevalaya - Voice Support Options\n\nThoughts board: IVR vs AI Voice Agent","x":-160,"y":-260,"width":460,"height":175,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"costopt","type":"text","text":"## Indicative Cost by Option\n\n*All figures approximate, vendor-quoted, and subject to change. To be verified directly with providers.*\n\n**Traditional IVR**\n- Monthly plans roughly Rs. 1,200 - 5,000 / month\n- Per-minute usage roughly Rs. 0.30 - 0.75 / min\n- Toll-free or virtual number rented separately\n\n**AI-IVR / End-to-End Voice Agent**\n- Usually per-minute; higher than IVR because of the AI stack (speech recognition + LLM + text-to-speech)\n- India-focused agents seen around $0.04 - 0.055 / min; wider market $0.01 - 1.00 / min\n- Enterprise platforms often quote custom pricing, sometimes with an annual commitment","x":1020,"y":200,"width":500,"height":510,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"trad","type":"text","text":"## Traditional IVR\n\n**What it is:** Keypad-driven menus (\"Press 1, Press 2\"). Routes calls; can self-serve simple structured tasks.\n\n**Strengths:**\n- Lowest per-call cost tier\n- Reliable and predictable\n- **Strong for high call volume routed across many departments.**\n\n**Limitations:**\n- Rigid menus; caller must map their problem onto the menu\n- Routes calls but does not resolve them\n- **It may end up with routing to human support**","x":480,"y":-460,"width":460,"height":480,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"aiivr","type":"text","text":"## AI-IVR (intent-based)\n\n**What it is:** Caller speaks naturally; the system detects intent and routes the call accordingly.\n\n**Strengths:**\n- Removes the rigid keypad menu\n- More natural entry point than traditional IVR\n\n**Limitations:**\n- Uses the same core technology as an end-to-end voice agent (speech recognition + NLP + text-to-speech)\n- Routes by intent but does not resolve the query itself\n- Effectively a routing-only subset of a full voice agent","x":480,"y":60,"width":460,"height":420,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"agent","type":"text","text":"## End-to-End AI Voice Agent\n\n**What it is:** A full conversational agent. Understands open-ended questions, answers and resolves them, escalates to a human only when needed. *Currently in use at DigiDevalaya.*\n\n**Strengths:**\n- Resolves routine queries directly, 24/7\n- Usually billed per minute of use\n- Scales during call spikes without adding staff\n\n**Limitations:**\n- Higher per-minute cost than traditional IVR\n- Quality depends on how well it is trained on the FAQs\n- Complex or sensitive issues still need a human","x":480,"y":520,"width":460,"height":475,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"billing","type":"text","text":"## How Voice Systems Are Charged.\n\nProviders typically use one of these models:\n\n**1. Per-minute** - pay for call minutes used. Often billed in 30-second pulses, so a 70-second call may bill as 90 seconds. Inbound and outbound are usually priced separately. International calls cost more.\n\n**2. Monthly plan** - a fixed fee, sometimes bundling a set number of free minutes.\n\n**3. Per-channel / concurrency** - pay for the number of simultaneous calls supported, not minutes used.\n\n**4. Per-agent / seat** - pay per support seat; common for contact-center platforms.\n\nNo amount is shown in any website, they ask for requesting the demo these are just approximate cost.","x":1020,"y":-340,"width":500,"height":500,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"weigh","type":"text","text":"## Points to Weigh\n\n- **Traditional IVR's main purpose is routing across many departments or agents; the current setup has 1-2 staff**\n- The current escalation flow already collects info and uses callbacks rather than live transfers\n- A callback model lets a small team batch responses instead of staffing a live phone line\n- Adding an IVR layer places a menu step before the existing conversational agent\n- Temple platforms may see call spikes around festivals - worth checking how each option handles a surge","x":1640,"y":-26,"width":480,"height":372,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"context","type":"text","text":"## Current Situation (Assumed)\n\n- Temple SaaS: Quires\n- ~50 users for application\n- 1-2 human support staff\n- Currently running: an end-to-end AI voice agent answering FAQs\n- **Escalation flow**: agent collects the issue and user details, then a human calls the user back","x":-160,"y":-85,"width":460,"height":285}
	],
